    "notes": {
        "7471b175-c8d9-4fc5-ba03-dd9a277736d7": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 288,
            "width": 672,
            "height": 224,
            "content": "## ⚠️ Timing\n\nThe query returns the row `id = 1` with `ts` = the current UNIX timestamp, so the row changes on every poll and WatchRows emits an `update` event.\n\nThe first poll after the flow starts is skipped and the start itself only records the baseline, so the trigger fires on the **second poll** after start. The AfterAll timeout (420 s) must stay longer than two tick intervals of the instance. No tables are needed."
        }
